"A circle of radius $k$ centered at the origin has the polar equation $r=k.$\n\nWe can compute the radius $k$ of our circle using the Pythagorean theorem, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{52}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the circle is $r=\\sqrt{52}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-325178/field-1/f8f12b478d0323f303a6e66b7a5ba6a7f9a8c130ea62fc433a4fcbcf716a57c6" :answer/id #uuid "c5b2cae2-321f-58dc-83ab-08b1cea647c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-325178/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "203a5109-baee-5991-bc8c-4149c669b848" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-325178/field-1/f8f12b478d0323f303a6e66b7a5ba6a7f9a8c130ea62fc433a4fcbcf716a57c6" :answer-field/choices ["q-325178/field-1/f8f12b478d0323f303a6e66b7a5ba6a7f9a8c130ea62fc433a4fcbcf716a57c6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-325178" :question/id #uuid "a020aa52-a41b-59b4-a523-caef6a0f3163" :question/math-academy-id "q-325178" :question/problem "The polar equation of the circle that is centered at the origin and that passes through the point $A(1,7)$ is$\\,\\,r=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "A circle of radius $k$ centered at the origin has the polar equation $r=k.$\n\nWe can compute the radius $k$ of our circle using the Pythagorean theorem, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{7}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+49} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{50} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the circle is $r=5\\sqrt{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-325178/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "47358248-2067-590e-80e1-5d20796434c5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["